the blind 20x20 fixture that started the issue is a multi-index site: true
a weighted key over several axes is a site: true
a key let-bound inside the body is followed to its remainder: true
an axis aliased one name at a time is followed too: true
a named function is read, not only an ~f argument: true
mod, Int.rem and a qualified ( % ) are remainders too: true
the Array.get spelling of an axis read is the same read: true
an axis read through a computed index counts as several axes: true
the flat spelling over a product length is a flat site: true
a flat closure spread over several lines is read whole: both remainders are sites: true
the positional Stdlib form and List.init are read too: true
a divisor that is a LEADING factor is not unflattening: true
a site converted onto the guard has no remainder left: true
one literal axis under a remainder is out of scope: true
unflattening by the trailing factor, or a trailing product, is the correct idiom: true
a flat length that is not a product at the call is out of scope: true
comments and string literals are not code: true
a remainder that reads the parameter only on its right is not a key: true
a remainder of values unrelated to the parameter is not a key: true
the site key is the remainder's source text with whitespace collapsed: true
one Site row absorbs one of two identical sites, and the other is refused: true
two Site rows absorb two identical sites: true
a File row absorbs every site of its file: true
a Site row for another file absorbs nothing, and is stale: true
a File row over a file with no sites is stale: true
shipping scanner refuses the blind hand-rolled fixture: true
shipping scanner accepts the fixture under a named exemption: true
shipping scanner accepts the fixture converted onto the guard: true
shipping scanner refuses the exemption the conversion left stale: true
shipping scanner reads the arrayjit test root too: true
shipping scanner refuses an emptied arrayjit source root: true
